# qtVlm - Virtual Loup de mer GUI

**A Qt-based application for virtual sailing and marine navigation**

[![License: GPL v3](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-GPLv3-blue.svg)](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0)
[![Platform](https://img.shields.io/badge/platform-Linux%20%7C%20Windows%20%7C%20macOS-lightgrey)](https://github.com/johla/qtVlm)

---

## Overview

qtVlm is a comprehensive sailing and navigation application that combines weather visualization, route planning, and virtual sailing capabilities. Whether you're planning a real voyage or competing in virtual regattas, qtVlm provides the tools you need.

### Key Features

🌊 **Weather Visualization**
- Display GRIB weather files on interactive maps
- Multiple weather parameters (wind, pressure, waves, temperature)
- Time-based weather animation
- Isobar and isotherm displays

⛵ **Virtual Sailing**
- Connect to Virtual Regatta (VLM) online platform
- Real-time race participation
- Opponent tracking
- Race rankings and statistics

🗺️ **Navigation Tools**
- Route planning with weather optimization
- Waypoint management (POI - Points of Interest)
- Great circle (orthodromic) calculations
- Distance and bearing measurements

📊 **Boat Performance**
- Polar diagram support
- Performance calculations based on weather
- Speed optimization
- VMG (Velocity Made Good) analysis

🧭 **Real Boat Support**
- GPS/NMEA data integration
- Track recording
- Real-time position display

---

## Quick Start

### Installation

**Linux:**
```bash
git clone https://github.com/johla/qtVlm.git
cd qtVlm
make
./qtVlm
```

**Windows:**
Download the latest release from the [Releases page](https://github.com/johla/qtVlm/releases)

**macOS:**
```bash
brew install qt@5
git clone https://github.com/johla/qtVlm.git
cd qtVlm
make
./qtVlm.app/Contents/MacOS/qtVlm
```

For detailed build instructions, see [BUILD_GUIDE.md](BUILD_GUIDE.md)

